<h1>Conveyor Guide Rails &amp; Side Rails</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">Conveyor guide rails, also called conveyor rails, side rails, or side guides, are side-mounted rails that keep products centered on the belt or roller surface, prevent edge falloff, create lanes for multi-row product flow, and orient products for downstream operations like labeling, printing, and case packing. Adjustable guide rail systems allow quick changeover between product sizes without tools, reducing downtime on multi-SKU packaging lines. Guide rails are one of the product handling categories in the <a href="/components/">conveyor components</a> map.</p>
<h2 id="types-heading">Types of Conveyor Guide Rails</h2>
<h3>Side Guide Rails</h3>
<p>Basic side containment rails mounted to the conveyor frame on both sides of the belt or roller surface. Keep products from falling off the conveyor edges during transport. Standard on most belt and <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/">roller conveyors</a>.</p>
<p class="tags"><span class="usa-tag">Edge Protection</span>
<span class="usa-tag">Product Centering</span></p>
<h3>Adjustable Guide Rails</h3>
<p>Guide rails with adjustment mechanisms that allow quick width changes for different product sizes. Essential for multi-SKU operations. Available with hand-knob clamps, hand-wheel cranks, or quick-release pins for different changeover needs.</p>
<p class="tags"><span class="usa-tag">Quick Changeover</span>
<span class="usa-tag">Multi-SKU</span></p>
<h3>Lane Dividers</h3>
<p>Internal guide rails that split a wide conveyor into multiple parallel lanes. Used to increase throughput, separate products, or create staging lanes before <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/case/">case packing</a> and <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/">palletizing</a>. Typically adjustable to accommodate different lane widths.</p>
<p class="tags"><span class="usa-tag">Multi-Lane</span>
<span class="usa-tag">Throughput</span></p>
<h3>Flexible Guide Rails</h3>
<p>Curved or bendable guide rails for curved conveyor sections, <a href="/conveyor-types/spiral-conveyors/">spiral conveyors</a>, and custom layouts. Made from flexible UHMW, spring steel with UHMW covers, or sectional designs that follow the conveyor curve.</p>
<p class="tags"><span class="usa-tag">Curved</span>
<span class="usa-tag">Spiral</span></p>
<h3>Top Hold-Down Rails</h3>
<p>Rails mounted above the conveyor surface to prevent light products from tipping, bouncing, or being displaced by air currents. Common on <a href="/conveyor-types/incline-conveyors/">incline conveyors</a> and high-speed lines. Often combined with side guides for complete containment.</p>
<p class="tags"><span class="usa-tag">Incline</span>
<span class="usa-tag">High-Speed</span></p>
<h3>Precision Guide Rails</h3>
<p>High-accuracy guide systems for positioning products before labelers, printers, vision systems, or <a href="/conveyor-functions/indexing-conveyors/">indexing conveyors</a>. Tighter tolerances (1/16" gap) and stiffer construction than standard transport guides.</p>
<p class="tags"><span class="usa-tag">Labeling</span>
<span class="usa-tag">Vision</span></p>
